WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.760
- These PVC tube instruments,

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.700
that is a three dollar piece of plastic

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.790
you can buy at Lowe's

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:09.180
and that is part of what's exciting

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:13.315
about how would someone, a musical being,

00:00:13.315 --> 00:00:14.980
look at this for the first time,

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.723
what would they want to do with it?

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.120
- The instruments come about,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.060
I think every one is a
little bit different.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.150
Anybody can bring an idea to the table.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.740
Our tone mill was one of our Blue Men

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.073
that drew a sketch.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.460
- The concept of this is
that you have different tubes

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.900
and then the length of the tube

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.343
is creating the pitch, the note.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.960
By having two, you can have a chord.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.210
Potentially, you can use a stick

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:52.020
or you can use another
tube that has its own note

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.183
to create a chord.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.480
This is another piece,

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.630
another instrument that we're working on

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:10.200
for a piece that's being developed

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.440
about feedback.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.690
There's a speaker on one end,

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:15.187
there's a microphone on the other end

00:01:15.187 --> 00:01:18.290
and you, when you put a
microphone at a speaker,

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.975
it causes feedback.

00:01:19.975 --> 00:01:24.975
And, with the pipe, we can
tune it to be different notes.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.520
Where the struggle is, is
that every day we walk in,

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.190
the notes are totally different.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.200
We're now being inspired by the challenge

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.800
to try and find a way to
make this actually workable

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.123
and tunable every night.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.510
So we're trying to find an instrument

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:54.040
that could drone in a
similar way as didgeridoo

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:57.190
but, obviously, have
different playing aspects

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:59.410
and something that was, again,

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:01.700
theatrically something that was visual

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.740
and had a lot of action to it.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:07.603
It's kind of inspired by a
hurdy-gurdy style instrument.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:12.930
You're bowing this and
then changing the note

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:13.933
with this lever.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:30.750
- Similar concept, we've
got two higher strings here,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.700
just music wire, something
you have on a piano.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.620
And, this wheel that you spin,

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.220
and then very sophisticated,

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:43.220
we have zip ties cut to a
little over a half an inch.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:48.460
And, when you rotate this,
you are plucking the strings

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.780
and then we have this
slider which is fretting

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:55.100
and we've come up with our
own musical language here,

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:58.040
the Blue Men speak in colors and shapes

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.193
when reading music.

00:03:12.183 --> 00:03:13.980
- So we basically took a vibraphone

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.720
and split it apart

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.720
onto a separate sort of playable platform

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.823
that can be a lot more
visual as an instrument.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:29.950
So these are actual vibraphone keys

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.420
and then there's pickups
underneath each one

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.210
so that we can now run it through

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:37.670
whatever fun pedals we want to do -

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.807
we want to run it through, so.

